  "title": "September 05 Weekly Field Notes — NVIDIA's Solar Throne, Proving Its Strength",
  "summary": "NVIDIA holds the Solar Throne at $5.56T in market cap, as semiconductor industry momentum dominated the weekly market.",
  "body": "<h3>No Change in the Solar Throne</h3><p>Last week, the order of the Universe remained stable. NVIDIA firmly held the Solar Throne with a market cap of $5.56T, maintaining the same position as the previous week. Apple ($4.68T) and Alphabet ($4.1T) followed, and the ranking of the top 5 planets remained unchanged.</p><h3>Semiconductor Sector Momentum Continues</h3><p>In weekly gains, semiconductor-related companies dominated the center of the Universe. Micron Technology recorded the highest gain at 7.1%, while NVIDIA rose 5.8% and Meta Platforms rose 5.4%. This reflects the market's sustained interest in AI and semiconductor demand.</p><h3>Declining Planets</h3><p>Meanwhile, in the decline rankings, Broadcom posted the largest drop at 3.9%. Amazon (-3.5%) and Eli Lilly (-2.7%) also showed weakness. Despite broad sector strength, some companies are entering a correction phase.</p><h3>Emerging Forces Worth Noting</h3><p>Arm Holdings has emerged as a rising company under observation, with KIOXIA Holdings Corporation (momentum 870), Seagate Technology (373), and Dell (325) showing strong momentum. While not yet entering the top rankings, they possess strong upward propulsion.</p><h3>The Universe's Order, Recorded in History</h3><p>This week clearly demonstrated the dominance of the technology and semiconductor sectors. Though the composition of the top 5 planets showed no change, sector-level volatility remained active, showing that new variables are preparing at the edges of the Universe. The Universe turns, and the record remains.</p><div class=\"col-chart\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 700 310\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><defs><linearGradient id=\"wg2\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"0\"><stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#9c7a3a\"/><stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#f2ba3c\"/></linearGradient></defs><rect width=\"700\" height=\"310\" fill=\"#10141f\"/><text x=\"26\" y=\"34\" fill=\"#f2ba3c\" font-size=\"19\" font-weight=\"800\">This Week's Stars — Blazing Stars and Fading Stars</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"56\" fill=\"#8a94b8\" font-size=\"12.5\" font-weight=\"600\">Earth TOP 20 Weekly Market Cap Change — Leaders and Laggards</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"95\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Micron Technolog</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"80\" width=\"380\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"url(#wg2)\"/><text x=\"590\" y=\"95\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">+7.1%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"128\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">NVIDIA</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"113\" width=\"310\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"url(#wg2)\"/><text x=\"520\" y=\"128\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">+5.8%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"161\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Meta Platforms (</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"146\" width=\"289\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"url(#wg2)\"/><text x=\"499\" y=\"161\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">+5.4%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Broadcom</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"178\" width=\"209\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#386ee1\"/><text x=\"419\" y=\"193\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">-3.9%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"226\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Amazon</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"211\" width=\"187\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#386ee1\"/><text x=\"397\" y=\"226\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">-3.5%</text><text x=\"26\" y=\"259\" fill=\"#e6ebfa\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"800\">Eli Lilly</text><rect x=\"200\" y=\"244\" width=\"145\" height=\"20\" rx=\"6\" fill=\"#386ee1\"/><text x=\"355\" y=\"259\" fill=\"#fff\" font-size=\"14.5\" font-weight=\"800\">-2.7%</text><text x=\"674\" y=\"296\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#9c7a3a\" font-size=\"11.5\" font-weight=\"800\">UNIVERTRIX · univertrix.com</text></svg></div><div class=\"col-chart\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 700 300\" xmlns=\"h